{"author":{"id":"6c7374a500bfd4cb191ae45b3f9d4b7a3d9d7f0324d04add217e8cbefeb7e1b9"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1793444693,"nonce":"ADxsYJuMZwQOssAmgw1eE+IXxwQ=","message":"**Cause, corrected**\n\nThe glyph shader (TextShader) already applies a record's local clip. The defect was in blinc_abi: a65b3a6 made the innermost rounded clip a record's local clip (clipping().cut), but Run::draw rebased only clip.local to each glyph's corner, so a glyph's cut clip stayed in absolute layout coordinates and clipped every glyph away.\n\n**Fix**\n\nblinc_abi 671ec8a rebases the cut clip per glyph (CI green on all three platforms). Ashui pin moved from the ashui-text branch to blinc_abi main at 671ec8a in 86ec1db: default and render lanes pass, NestedClipTextPixels included, no uncaught exceptions.\n\n**Still to check**\n\nBox, image and backdrop records take the same local clip with their own origin; NestedRoundedClipPixels passes, but a scroll view cutting a circle (the blinc_abi 77fc7dc case) is not covered by an ashui test yet.\n\nClose once 86ec1db is pushed.","files":null}]}